## apollo → nwk1 (`https://system.bbimarketing.com/new/api/`)

POST auth must equal `$randomStringConstructor` (`api/index.php:659`). Fail → **401** `"Unauthorized"` (`:882`). Unknown `type` → **400** `{status:failure,results:…}`.

### `type=pollingInfoRequest` (`:664-735`)

**Caller:** `projects/apollo/services/pulse_fetch/core/polling.php:10-31` (SSL **verify on**).

POST: `auth`, `type=pollingInfoRequest`. Optional: `cid`, `store_numbers[]`, `orderBy=store_number` (apollo kickoff sends none of these).

nwk1: companies with `rd_available='1'`; locations with `vpn_ip_address IS NOT NULL`; creds = location `vpn_custom_*` else company `poll_username`/`poll_password`. Push stores (`pulse_version=4`) if a zip exists under `/var/www/upload.bbimarketing.com/dominos-uploaded` matching `^[^-]+-(\d{5})_`.

```json
{"status":"ok","results":[{"store_number","client_name","vpn_ip_address","username","password","pulse_version"}]}
```

Apollo inserts into `daily_polling` (does **not** persist `pulse_version`).

### `type=nllProvider` (`:737-740` → `nllProvider.inc`)

| `request` | Lines | Extra POST | Returns |
|---|---|---|---|
| `1` | `:7` | — | NLL-enabled stores + `nll_settings` tuples |
| `2` | `:78` | — | test-file seed rows |
